# Line-ending policy.
#
# Shell scripts run under bash (Cygwin / MSYS2 / Linux) and MUST be LF —
# CRLF makes bash fail with "$'\r': command not found" and syntax errors
# at `case ... in`. Pin them to LF so they stay correct even when a
# Windows checkout has core.autocrlf=true.
*.sh    text eol=lf

# Linker scripts and the modules manifest are read by the toolchain; LF.
*.ld    text eol=lf

# PowerShell scripts are Windows-native; keep CRLF.
*.ps1   text eol=crlf
